2026-11-24 - Admin panel: Blog articles with add / edit / delete (CRUD)
------------------------------------------------------------------
GOAL: blog articles could only be changed by editing HTML files. Now the admin panel has a
"Blog articles" section: list, create, edit, delete. Same idea as Products:
   admin form -> database (MongoDB) -> "publish" writes the static website files.

NEW FILES (admin-server/)
  models/BlogPost.js          what an article is (title, address/slug, date, text, FAQ, picture, SEO fields).
  services/blogPublish.js     the publisher. For every PUBLISHED article it writes <slug>/index.html from the
                              template, rebuilds the card grid in blog.html, updates sitemap.xml and writes
                              blog-posts.json (list of live articles). Drafts and deleted articles lose their page.
                              Before writing it backs up blog.html, sitemap.xml, blog-posts.json to backups/ and
                              puts them back if anything fails. It refuses an address that belongs to another part
                              of the site (e.g. "bmi", "contact"). Article text is cleaned: scripts, iframes,
                              event handlers, javascript: links and unsafe styles are removed.
  services/blogImport.js      reads the 3 existing articles (title, text, FAQ, dates...) so the admin can take them over.
  routes/blog.js              the API: GET/POST /api/blog, GET/PUT/DELETE /api/blog/:slug, POST /import, POST /publish.
                              Login required. After a save the site updates by itself (AUTO_PUBLISH=false in .env
                              switches to a "Publish to website" button).
  templates/blog-article.html the page shell (header, styles, footer) with {{TOKENS}}; made from the PVD article by
  templates/organization.json   scripts/makeBlogTemplate.js. Re-run that script if the header/footer of an article
                              page changes (e.g. a new address), so new articles get the same one.
  views/admin/blog.html + blog.js   the screens: list, editor with text toolbar (heading, bold, lists, links, "edit
                              as HTML"), picture upload, FAQ rows, Google title/description.
CHANGED
  server.js (mounts /api/blog), views/admin/admin.js (sidebar link), views/admin/pages.js (hides the old
  "blog cards" fields in Pages > Blog page, since cards now come from the Blog section),
  ../build_pages.js (the sitemap it writes reads blog-posts.json, so a product publish keeps the articles).

FIRST USE: open Admin > Blog articles > "Import the existing articles". Then publish by saving any article.
The first publish rewrites blog.html's cards (the old per-card CMS tags are dropped on purpose).

TESTED: no MongoDB on this PC, so the database was replaced by an in-memory stand-in. With it: parse + re-render of all
3 articles matches the live pages; publish/delete/clash/rollback (33 checks pass); the real routes and screens driven in
a browser (import, create, validation, edit, delete). NOT tested: real MongoDB, Cloudinary upload, the live server.
LIMITS: the page address cannot be changed after creation (it would break links); menus inside new article pages are a
copy and are not refreshed when the product catalog changes (same as the existing 3 articles).

2026-11-24 (later) - Blog editor: full text formatting
The article text editor is now views/admin/blog-editor.js (own file; blog.js just mounts it). Toolbar: undo/redo, text style
(Paragraph, Heading 2/3/4, Quote), size, bold, italic, underline, strike-through, text colour, highlight colour, "back to normal
colour", align left/centre/right/justify, bullet + numbered lists, link / unlink / LINK COLOUR, tables (choose rows, columns,
heading row; then + row above/below, + column left/right, - row, - column, delete table), divider line, pictures inside the
text (upload), clear formatting, and an "HTML" view. Colours and sizes are saved as inline styles (style="color: ..."), so
they survive in the published page. Enter now makes real <p> paragraphs.
Server side (services/blogPublish.js): the cleaner now also allows h4, strike/del, mark, tables with captions/footers,
colspan/rowspan/scope, borders, vertical-align, and turns <font color> into a span; still strips scripts, event handlers,
javascript: links, url() / expression() styles. Pictures inside the text: uploads/ files are copied into assets/blog/uploads/
and site paths get the "../" an article page needs.
Article pages got styles for tables, quotes, dividers, pictures, highlights, h4 (templates/blog-article.html, built by
scripts/makeBlogTemplate.js - re-run it after changing the header/footer of an article page).
Tested in a browser with the in-memory stand-in: heading, colour, link, link colour, size, bold, highlight, alignment, table
(+row, +column), divider, quote all saved and published correctly; 12 cleaner checks and the 33 publish checks pass.

